  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="ad91-f7b2-19da-12a1" name="Later Carthaginian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #30 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). 270 BC to 203 BC This list covers the armies of Carthage during the time of the city’s conflict with Rome. Carthaginian forces were varied and complex and we have chosen to concentrate on the armies employed in Spain, and in Hannibal’s invasion of Italy. There are many mercenary contingents but unusually, the Allies and Mercenaries rule does not apply to them. Units that are available only in one theatre are marked appropriately, as (S)pain only or (I)taly only. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Later Carthaginian]
  Cavalry: up to 30%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 30% Infantry: At least 50% Elephants: 0-1 per 1000 points</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
